cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Tell or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Tell: a tracker of institutional distress in U.S. higher education, built on Recursive Information-Container Dynamics (RICD)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Speer
    given-names: Carmen
repository-code: "https://github.com/carmen-speer/RICD-Tell"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-20
keywords:
  - higher education
  - college closure
  - institutional distress
  - early warning
  - feedback divergence
  - Recursive Information-Container Dynamics
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Tell reads the divergence between how an institution represents itself
  (its official channel) and what its own financial and enrollment records
  show (its operational channel), and combines it with institutional size,
  sector and anchoring to flag distress. Tracker v3 passed a pre-registered,
  out-of-sample test on 987 held-out U.S. institutions (closures 2019 to
  2025). The theory it implements, RICD, is in docs/ (the RICD 17.7 Spine
  and Catalog). Every protocol, run, result and erratum is in this
  repository.
